.TH M3U8-DOWNLOADER 1 "July 2026" "m3u8-downloader 5.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
m3u8-downloader \- download, filter, and merge m3u8 streams
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B m3u8-downloader
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ url ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B m3u8-downloader
opens the terminal UI when run without a URL. When a URL is provided, it
downloads supported media or a regular Bilibili video page. HLS playlists can
be filtered by keyword or regular expression, and downloaded content is merged
into an MP4 file with FFmpeg.
.PP
The command supports media playlists directly and master playlists with multiple
variants. By default, the highest bandwidth variant is selected unless a variant
index is specified.
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.I url
Optional media URL or regular Bilibili video page. If omitted, the terminal UI
is opened.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-h, \--help
Show command help and exit.
.TP
.BI \-o " OUTPUT"
.TQ
.BI \--output " OUTPUT"
Write the merged MP4 file to
.IR OUTPUT .
.TP
.BI \--work-dir " WORK_DIR"
Directory used for downloaded TS segments. The directory is created if needed.
.TP
.BI \--header " HEADER"
Add an HTTP request header. Use the form
.IR "Name: value" .
This option can be repeated. A common use is passing a Referer header.
.TP
.BI \--cookie " COOKIE"
Set the Bilibili Cookie for a Bilibili download. This value takes precedence
over the saved Bilibili Cookie configuration.
.TP
.BI \--page " PAGE"
Select one Bilibili page number, starting at 1.
.TP
.B \--all-pages
Download all pages from a multi-page Bilibili video.
.TP
.BI \--quality " QUALITY"
Set the maximum Bilibili quality ID, for example 80.
.TP
.BI \--video-codec " CODEC"
Set Bilibili video codec preference. Choices are
.BR avc ,
.BR hevc , and
.BR av1 .
Repeat the option to provide a preference order.
.TP
.BI \--audio-language " LANGUAGE"
Prefer the specified Bilibili audio language code.
.TP
.B \--hdr
Prefer HDR video when available.
.TP
.B \--no-subtitles
Do not save or mux Bilibili subtitles.
.TP
.B \--no-cover
Do not save the Bilibili cover image.
.TP
.B \--save-danmaku
Save the Bilibili danmaku XML file.
.TP
.B \--no-chapters
Do not write Bilibili chapters.
.TP
.B \--no-info
Do not save the Bilibili information JSON file.
.TP
.B \--keep-bilibili-tracks
Keep the downloaded Bilibili video and audio temporary files.
.TP
.BI \--keyword " KEYWORD"
Filter out segments whose URL or title contains
.IR KEYWORD .
This option can be repeated.
.TP
.B \--regex
Treat filter keywords as regular expressions instead of plain text.
.TP
.BI \--threads " THREADS"
Number of concurrent segment download workers.
.TP
.BI \--variant " VARIANT"
Select a master playlist variant by zero-based index. If omitted, the highest
bandwidth variant is used.
.TP
.BI \--dump-filtered " DUMP_FILTERED"
Write the filtered m3u8 playlist to
.I DUMP_FILTERED
before downloading. This is useful for checking which segments remain after
filtering.
.TP
.B \--keep-segments
Keep downloaded TS segment files after the MP4 merge finishes.
.TP
.B \--tui
Open the terminal UI explicitly.
.SH EXAMPLES
.SS Open the terminal UI
.EX
m3u8-downloader
.EE
.SS Basic download
.EX
m3u8-downloader "https://example.com/video/index.m3u8" -o video.mp4
.EE
.SS Use a Referer header
.EX
m3u8-downloader "https://example.com/video.m3u8" \
  -o video.mp4 \
  --header "Referer: https://example.com/"
.EE
.SS Increase download concurrency
.EX
m3u8-downloader "https://example.com/video.m3u8" -o video.mp4 --threads 16
.EE
.SS Filter ad segments by keywords
.EX
m3u8-downloader "https://example.com/video.m3u8" \
  -o video.mp4 \
  --keyword /video/adjump/
.EE
.SS Filter with regular expressions and inspect the playlist
.EX
m3u8-downloader "https://example.com/video.m3u8" \
  -o video.mp4 \
  --keyword "adjump|banner|promo" \
  --regex \
  --dump-filtered filtered.m3u8
.EE
.SS Select a master playlist variant
.EX
m3u8-downloader "https://example.com/master.m3u8" -o video.mp4 --variant 0
.EE
.SS Download a Bilibili video
.EX
m3u8-downloader "https://www.bilibili.com/video/BV..." \
  --cookie "SESSDATA=..." \
  --page 2 \
  --quality 80 \
  --video-codec avc \
  --output lesson.mp4
.EE
.SS Download all Bilibili pages and save attachments
.EX
m3u8-downloader "https://www.bilibili.com/video/BV..." \
  --all-pages \
  --save-danmaku \
  --output ./downloads
.EE
.SS Choose Bilibili codec order and disable attachments
.EX
m3u8-downloader "https://www.bilibili.com/video/BV..." \
  --video-codec hevc \
  --video-codec avc \
  --no-subtitles \
  --no-cover \
  --no-chapters \
  --no-info
.EE
.SS Keep downloaded segment files
.EX
m3u8-downloader "https://example.com/video.m3u8" \
  -o video.mp4 \
  --work-dir ./segments \
  --keep-segments
.EE
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/m3u8-downloader/config.json
Desktop application configuration file.
.TP
.I /usr/share/m3u8-downloader/
Installed application source and shared files in the Debian package.
.SH REQUIREMENTS
The Debian package depends on Python 3, requests, aiohttp, PyQt6, Textual, VLC,
and FFmpeg. FFmpeg must be available for MP4 merging.
